=== PARITY (vs web DriveScoreWidget.tsx) ===
  Data sources -> bound via the shared state-holder seam (DriveScoreSource -> DriveScoreModel):
    useFleetAnalytics(7) (avg_efficiency_wh_km + isLoading/isFetching/isStale/isError/dataUpdatedAt/refetch),
    useUnits (unitPrefs.distance), useTranslation. The view performs NO HTTP.
  Projection -> DriveScoreProjection.compute is a 1:1 port of the web derivation:
      efficiency = analytics?.avg_efficiency_wh_km ?? 0
      score      = efficiency > 0 ? min(100, round(250 / efficiency * 100)) : 0
      display    = unitPrefs.distance == 'mi' ? whPerKm * 1.609344 : whPerKm   (unit 'Wh/mi' | 'Wh/km')
      color band = score > 75 #10b981 · score > 50 #f59e0b · else #ef4444 (exact web hex)
    Verified by the executed binary (score 320/460/700 km -> 78/54/36; clamp 100; nil/0 -> 0;
    band breaks at 76/75/51/50; mi conversion 320 -> 515 Wh/mi; fmtNumber grouping 1234.6 -> "1,235").
  Composition -> title-less glass shell (web WidgetShell with no title -> overlay freshness): header =
    freshness chip + refresh (+ optional Open). Content = WidgetGaugeHero parity: a radial ring (track +
    band-tinted value arc from 12 o'clock, centered score, "Score" caption) and, when not compact, the
    "Efficiency <value> <Wh/mi|Wh/km>" stat. Compact (1x1) renders the gauge only (web `isCompact`).
  Shared components -> web EmptyState -> ContentUnavailableView ("No data yet"); web RadialGauge -> native
    Circle().trim arc; web DataFreshness -> DriveScoreFreshnessChip; web Skeleton -> TSSkeleton. Tokens are
    the real SI design system (Color.TS / Font.TS / TSSpacing / TSRadius / TSMotion), compiled against the
    real apps/design/generated/apple/Tokens.swift in the typecheck below. Recharts -> none / Leaflet -> none.
  States (all render) -> loading (skeleton chrome) · content (gauge hero) · empty ("No data yet") · error
    (retry affordance) · stale (amber chip + "Reconnecting" banner) · offline (cached value + muted chip +
    "Offline" banner). Phase resolution keeps cached content visible behind refresh/errors (web shell).
  i18n -> all source keys resolve through the P1/S10 facade with the web t(key,default) fallback:
    widget.score, widget.efficiency, widget.noScore -> ALL PRESENT in DriveScoreWidget.strings (+ registry
    widget.driveScore[.description] + native chrome/freshness/a11y keys). No English literals in native code.
  a11y -> gauge hero carries a single combined VoiceOver summary (DriveScoreAccessibility.gaugeSummary:
    "Score <n> out of 100. Efficiency <v> <unit>"); refresh / retry / open each carry an accessibilityLabel;
